From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] feat(dev): add always-on failure log
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dev only, not for release builds.

Problem: a game presented at ~90 FPS with a black window and nothing in the
logs; failures returned to the game (E_FAIL sources, skipped draws, device
loss) were silent unless VKD3D_DEBUG was raised (N§21).

Root cause: n/a (diagnostic).

Fix: C:\gfx-failures.log, one file per bottle shared with MoltenVK, one line
per event (time, exe and pid, category). Each distinct message, with numbers
and hex collapsed, is written in full 3 times, then summarised as
"repeat: +N more" every 10 s. Categories: error / fixme (every ERR and
FIXME, regardless of VKD3D_DEBUG), create-failed (device Create* returning a
failure, with the resource description), info (cached PSO blob rejected),
draw-skipped, device-removed (N§22).

Verified by: on the demo, lines from both layers; its create-failed lines are
all stale cached PSO blobs (N§22).

Off switch: VKD3D_FAILURE_LOG=0 (or a path to write elsewhere).
